UserNamePasswordAuthenticatioFilter:
------------------------------------
UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter is a Spring Security filter that handles form-based login authentication using a username and password. It’s 
part of the default security filter chain in Spring Security.

What does it do?
----------------
Intercepts login requests (usually POST /login).
Extracts username and password from the request.
Creates an Authentication object (usually UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken).
Passes it to the AuthenticationManager for validation.
If authentication succeeds → calls successfulAuthentication().
If authentication fails → calls unsuccessfulAuthentication().



